t throughout','The interlocutor argues that the position entails three objects; the next counterexample answers it. No philosophical correction follows merely because the claim is being refuted.')],282:[('five body components / all four of his limbs, and his head','Change four to five','Four limbs plus one head accounts for five components, confirmed by the immediately following body-parts analogy at 283–284. The first description is distributed, not an arithmetic error.'),("ma yin par thal / wouldn't be",'Remove the negative or assign supplied you to a nonexistent pronoun','This is the negated consequence in the counterexample, with negative affix and modal/copular English support. The source licenses the negative; the supplied you is a rhetorical expansion.'),("'o na / Well now",'Rewrite Well now as a mandatory dictionary alternative','The current discourse transition is defensible; dictionary alternatives are contextual options, not textual emendation instructions.')]}
